% What the item is.
rule vitd_assay with provenance Article A57484,
        confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy":
an item is a vitamin D assay
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["82306", "82652"].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The articles: which HCPCS code each ICD-10 group serves.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

the article of first coast lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A56841, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of cgs lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A56798, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of wps lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A57484, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of wps lists HCPCS code "82652" in group 2,
    as stated in Article A57484, confer "82652 (group 1): Vit d 1 25-dihydroxy".
the article of noridian lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A57718, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of noridian lists HCPCS code "82652" in group 2,
    as stated in Article A57718, confer "82652 (group 1): Vit d 1 25-dihydroxy".
the article of wellpoint lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A57736, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of wellpoint lists HCPCS code "82652" in group 2,
    as stated in Article A57736, confer "82652 (group 1): Vit d 1 25-dihydroxy".
the article of palmetto lists HCPCS code "82306" in group 1,
    as stated in Article A59170, confer "82306 (group 1): Vitamin d 25 hydroxy".
the article of palmetto lists HCPCS code "82652" in group 2,
    as stated in Article A59170, confer "82652 (group 1): Vit d 1 25-dihydroxy".

% The six loaded tables, read one per jurisdiction.
rule vitd_table_first_coast with provenance Article A56841,
        confer "The submitted medical record must support the use of the selected ICD-10-CM code(s)":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of first coast
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A56841" as a description under table first_coast_icd10.

rule vitd_table_cgs with provenance Article A56798,
        confer "The diagnosis code(s) must best describe the patient's condition for which the service was performed":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of cgs
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A56798" as a description under table cgs_icd10.

rule vitd_table_wps with provenance Article A57484,
        confer "The diagnosis code(s) must best describe the patient's condition for which the service was performed":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of wps
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A57484" as a description under table wps_icd10.

rule vitd_table_noridian with provenance Article A57718,
        confer "When the documentation does not meet the criteria for the service rendered or the documentation does not establish the medical necessity for the services, such services will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of noridian
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A57718" as a description under table noridian_icd10.

rule vitd_table_wellpoint with provenance Article A57736,
        confer "The diagnosis code(s) must best describe the patient's condition for which the service was performed":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of wellpoint
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A57736" as a description under table wellpoint_icd10.

rule vitd_table_palmetto with provenance Article A59170,
        confer "The diagnosis code(s) must best describe the patient's condition for which the service was performed":
ICD10 code a code is listed in group a group of the article of palmetto
    if ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A59170" as a description under table palmetto_icd10.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The covered indication: the diagnosis code in the article's group for the
% HCPCS code, or a condition the LCD names in prose that the table has no
% code for (the 25-hydroxy assay only).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% a device of this model: the article's table read for the group that
% serves the code billed
rule vitd_indication_by_code:
a beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code a code in a jurisdiction
    if the article of the jurisdiction lists HCPCS code the code in group a group
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is an other code
    and ICD10 code the other code is listed in group the group of the article of the jurisdiction.

% a device of this model: the conditions each LCD names in prose that its
% article codes nowhere, stated below with their passages
rule vitd_indication_in_text:
a beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code "82306" in a jurisdiction
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is an indication in the text of the LCD of the jurisdiction.

low exposure to sunlight is an indication in the text of the LCD of cgs,
    as stated in LCD L33996, confer "low exposure to sunlight".
pregnancy is an indication in the text of the LCD of palmetto,
    as stated in LCD L39391, confer "Pregnant and lactating women".
lactation is an indication in the text of the LCD of palmetto,
    as stated in LCD L39391, confer "Pregnant and lactating women".

% Screening: the encounter-for-screening diagnosis codes (a device of this
% model: Z00.0-, Z00.8, Z13.2-), excluded by the five LCDs that say so.
rule vitd_screening:
a claim is for routine screening
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and the code is in ["Z00.00", "Z00.01", "Z00.8", "Z13.21", "Z13.228", "Z13.29"].

rule vitd_screening_excluded:
a claim is excluded as screening in a jurisdiction
    if routine screening is excluded by the jurisdiction
    and the claim is for routine screening.

routine screening is excluded by cgs,
    as stated in LCD L33996, confer "Vitamin D testing may not be used for routine screening".
routine screening is excluded by wps,
    as stated in LCD L34658, confer "Vitamin D testing may not be used for routine screening".
routine screening is excluded by noridian,
    as stated in LCD L36692, confer "Testing may not be used for routine or other screening".
routine screening is excluded by wellpoint,
    as stated in LCD L37535, confer "Testing may not be used for routine or other screening".
routine screening is excluded by palmetto,
    as stated in LCD L39391, confer "Reimbursement is not allowed for routine screening for vitamin D deficiency in asymptomatic individuals and/or during general encounters".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Osteoporosis under Noridian and Wellpoint: covered "if" one of the five
% conditions is documented.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% a device of this model: the osteoporosis codes without a current
% pathological fracture
rule vitd_osteoporosis_codes:
a code is an osteoporosis code
    if the code is in ["M81.0", "M81.6", "M81.8"].

% a diagnosis other than osteoporosis: nothing more to meet (a device)
rule vitd_osteoporosis_not_applicable:
a beneficiary meets the osteoporosis conditions of a jurisdiction
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is an osteoporosis code.

rule vitd_osteoporosis_noridian with provenance LCD L36692,
        confer "osteoporosis if":
a beneficiary meets the osteoporosis conditions of noridian
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and the code is an osteoporosis code
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of noridian.

rule vitd_osteoporosis_wellpoint with provenance LCD L37535,
        confer "osteoporosis if:":
a beneficiary meets the osteoporosis conditions of wellpoint
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and the code is an osteoporosis code
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of wellpoint.

qualifying bone density score is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of noridian,
    as stated in LCD L36692, confer "T score on DEXA scan".
history of fragility fractures is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of noridian,
    as stated in LCD L36692, confer "History of fragility fractures".
qualifying fracture risk assessment is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of noridian,
    as stated in LCD L36692, confer "FRAX > 3".
initiation of bisphosphonate therapy is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of noridian,
    as stated in LCD L36692, confer "Initiating bisphosphanate therapy".
qualifying bone density score is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of wellpoint,
    as stated in LCD L37535, confer "T score on DEXA scan".
history of fragility fractures is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of wellpoint,
    as stated in LCD L37535, confer "History of fragility fractures".
qualifying fracture risk assessment is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of wellpoint,
    as stated in LCD L37535, confer "FRAX> 3".
initiation of bisphosphonate therapy is a qualifying osteoporosis condition of wellpoint,
    as stated in LCD L37535, confer "Initiating bisphosphanate therapy".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Frequency: what the record of earlier tests shows. Devices of this model:
% the year is the 365 days before the date of service; the "24 hour period"
% is the calendar day.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule vitd_tests_in_year:
the number of vitamin D tests of a beneficiary in the year before a claim is a number
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the number is the count of each other date such that
        the beneficiary had a vitamin D test on the other date
        and the date is a number N days after the other date
        and N >= 0
        and N <= 365.

rule vitd_same_day:
a claim repeats a vitamin D test on the same day
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the beneficiary had a vitamin D test on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number < 1.

rule vitd_repeat:
a claim is a repeat vitamin D test
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had a vitamin D test on a date.

rule vitd_repeat_stable_normal:
a claim is a repeat test of a stable beneficiary in the normal range
    if the claim is a repeat vitamin D test
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the most recent vitamin D level of the beneficiary is a number ng per ml
    and the number >= 20
    and the number <= 50
    and the beneficiary is clinically stable.

% the WPS conditions with four tests a year: rickets and its sequelae,
% vitamin D deficiency, osteomalacia and aluminum bone disease, by code
rule vitd_wps_deficiency_codes with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "rickets, vitamin D deficiency, osteomalacia, and aluminum bone disease":
a code is a code of the deficiency conditions of wps
    if the code is in ["E55.0", "E55.9", "E64.3", "M83.0", "M83.1", "M83.2", "M83.3", "M83.4", "M83.5", "M83.8", "M83.9"].

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: clinical diagnostic
% laboratory tests (Claims Processing Manual chapter 16, which the LCD
% refers to), not durable medical equipment — no home is needed.
rule vitd_codes with provenance Article A57484,
        confer "82652 (group 1): Vit d 1 25-dihydroxy":
the policy for code a code is vitamin_d
    if the code is in ["82306", "82652"].

section applicability is:

vitamin_d has no specific documentation requirements.

rule vitd_benefit with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "Please refer to CMS IOM Publication 100-04, Medicare Claims Processing Manual , Chapter 16, Section 120.1 for additional limitations for Vitamin D assay testing":
the benefit category of code a code is diagnostic laboratory tests
    if the policy for code the code is vitamin_d.

section question is:

% The claim is decided under the LCD of its jurisdiction: a device of this
% model (the contractor's jurisdiction is a fact of the claim).
rule vitd_rn:
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the jurisdiction of the claim is a contractor
    and the claim is reasonable and necessary in the contractor.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% One rule per LCD: a covered indication of that contractor's article or
% LCD, not screening, within that LCD's frequency limits.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule vitd_first_coast with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "The measurement of 25(OH) Vitamin D levels will be considered medically reasonable and necessary for patients with any of the following conditions":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in first coast
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in first coast
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in first coast
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of first coast.

rule vitd_cgs with provenance LCD L33996,
        confer "Indications: Measurement of vitamin D levels is indicated for patients with":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in cgs
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in cgs
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in cgs
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of cgs.

rule vitd_wps with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "Indications: Measurement of vitamin D levels is indicated for patients with":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in wps
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in wps
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in wps
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of wps.

rule vitd_noridian with provenance LCD L36692,
        confer "Measurement of 25-OH Vitamin D level is indicated for patients with":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in noridian
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in noridian
    and the beneficiary meets the osteoporosis conditions of noridian
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in noridian
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of noridian.

rule vitd_wellpoint with provenance LCD L37535,
        confer "Measurement of 25-OH Vitamin D level is indicated for patients with":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in wellpoint
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in wellpoint
    and the beneficiary meets the osteoporosis conditions of wellpoint
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in wellpoint
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of wellpoint.

rule vitd_palmetto with provenance LCD L39391,
        confer "25-hydroxyvitamin D [25(OH)D] testing will be considered medically reasonable and necessary for individuals at risk for deficiency with the following conditions":
a claim is reasonable and necessary in palmetto
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a vitamin D assay
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a covered indication for HCPCS code the code in palmetto
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is excluded as screening in palmetto
    and the claim is within the frequency limits of palmetto.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Frequency limits, LCD by LCD.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% First Coast: one level per 24 hours; three tests per year; one per year
% once supplemented to normal levels.
rule vitd_frequency_first_coast with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "Limitations":
a claim is within the frequency limits of first coast
    if the claim is within the daily limit of first coast
    and the claim is within the yearly limit of first coast.

rule vitd_daily_first_coast with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "Only one 25 OH Vitamin D level will be reimbursed in any 24 hour period":
a claim is within the daily limit of first coast
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim repeats a vitamin D test on the same day.

rule vitd_yearly_first_coast with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "It’s not reasonable and necessary to perform more than three tests per year":
a claim is within the yearly limit of first coast
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 2.

rule vitd_yearly_first_coast_supplemented with provenance LCD L33771,
        confer "Patients with Vitamin D deficiency that have been supplemented to normal levels are limited to one test per year":
a claim is within the yearly limit of first coast
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 0.

% CGS: no number; once replacement is accomplished, annual testing.
rule vitd_frequency_cgs with provenance LCD L33996,
        confer "Once a beneficiary has been shown to be vitamin D deficient, further testing is medically necessary only to ensure adequate replacement has been accomplished":
a claim is within the frequency limits of cgs
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels.

rule vitd_frequency_cgs_annual with provenance LCD L33996,
        confer "Thereafter, annual testing may be appropriate depending upon the indication and other mitigating factors":
a claim is within the frequency limits of cgs
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 0.

% WPS: one level per 24 hours; once a year, or four times a year for
% rickets, vitamin D deficiency, osteomalacia and aluminum bone disease.
rule vitd_frequency_wps with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "Utilization Guidelines":
a claim is within the frequency limits of wps
    if the claim is within the daily limit of wps
    and the claim is within the yearly limit of wps.

rule vitd_daily_wps with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "Only one 25 OH vitamin D level will be reimbursed in any 24 hour period":
a claim is within the daily limit of wps
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim repeats a vitamin D test on the same day.

rule vitd_yearly_wps_other with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "Assays of vitamin D levels for conditions other than for rickets, vitamin D deficiency, osteomalacia, and aluminum bone disease will be limited to once a year":
a claim is within the yearly limit of wps
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is a code of the deficiency conditions of wps
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 0.

rule vitd_yearly_wps_deficiency with provenance LCD L34658,
        confer "Assays of the appropriate vitamin D levels for rickets, vitamin D deficiency, osteomalacia, and aluminum bone disease will be limited to 4 per year":
a claim is within the yearly limit of wps
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and the code is a code of the deficiency conditions of wps
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 3.

% Noridian: no number; a repeat test of a clinically stable beneficiary in
% the 20-50 ng/ml range needs documentation of its necessity.
rule vitd_frequency_noridian with provenance LCD L36692,
        confer "If Vitamin D level is between 20 and 50 ng/ml and patient is clinically stable, repeat testing is often unnecessary":
a claim is within the frequency limits of noridian
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is a repeat test of a stable beneficiary in the normal range.

rule vitd_frequency_noridian_documented with provenance LCD L36692,
        confer "if performed, documentation most clearly indicate the necessity of the test":
a claim is within the frequency limits of noridian
    if the claim is a repeat test of a stable beneficiary in the normal range
    and the record clearly indicates the necessity of the test of the claim.

% Wellpoint: the same limitation, in its own words.
rule vitd_frequency_wellpoint with provenance LCD L37535,
        confer "If Vitamin D level is between 20 and 50 ng/ml and patient is clinically stable, repeat testing is often unnecessary":
a claim is within the frequency limits of wellpoint
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is a repeat test of a stable beneficiary in the normal range.

rule vitd_frequency_wellpoint_documented with provenance LCD L37535,
        confer "if performed, documentation must clearly indicate the necessity of the test":
a claim is within the frequency limits of wellpoint
    if the claim is a repeat test of a stable beneficiary in the normal range
    and the record clearly indicates the necessity of the test of the claim.

% Palmetto: no number; once replacement is accomplished, annual testing
% whose need the documentation supports.
rule vitd_frequency_palmetto with provenance LCD L39391,
        confer "Once a beneficiary has been shown to be vitamin D deficient with a serum level of":
a claim is within the frequency limits of palmetto
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels.

rule vitd_frequency_palmetto_annual with provenance LCD L39391,
        confer "The documentation must support the need for annual testing":
a claim is within the frequency limits of palmetto
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has been supplemented to normal vitamin D levels
    and the number of vitamin D tests of the beneficiary in the year before the claim is a number
    and the number <= 0
    and the record clearly indicates the necessity of the test of the claim.
